Let the page hold a key down for the scripts

Scripts hear of keys as they are pressed and let go of (HOOK_KEYPRESS)
and ask whether one is held (key_pressed). The one that lights up what
lies on the ground is read that way. A touch screen has no key to hold:
the page can now press one for the scripts alone and let go of it again,
so that a button can switch the lighting on and off. The game's own
keyboard handling never sees that key, so nothing else typed turns into
its shifted self while it is down.
